# 🔴 READ THIS BEFORE PINNING a657f4f OR ANYTHING AFTER IT. Not a plain pin: the ORDER of
# operations matters, and getting it wrong leaves twelve kommune codes unresolved with
# everything green.
upgrade_order_from_a657f4f: >-
  a657f4f contains 3e72760, which widens the Klass ingest window from 1960 back to 1950. The
  twelve orphan kommune codes all dissolved ON OR BEFORE 1960, so the old window could never
  see them — the ingest was not failing, it was not looking far enough back. The sequence is
  therefore DEPLOY, then `klass_refresh` ON THE NEW IMAGE, then transform. A transform before
  the refresh runs against the old window and resolves nothing. ops-dev corrected its own
  earlier answer to add this (#1367), so do not carry over the plain "deploy then transform"
  shape from previous pins. Anything pinned after a657f4f inherits this requirement unless
  atlas says the refresh has already run everywhere.

release_when: >-
  ops-dev or imac reports a specific tag as DEPLOYED and nominates it. The clearing event is
  somebody else's verdict arriving, never this agent deciding the gap looks small. ops-dev has
  said it will nominate a657f4f as LANDED if all eight ssb-06913 series come back at 357, and
  will otherwise name what is short. Re-run --drift before acting: the tags above will have
  aged.

carry_forward: >-
